2026-10-15 17:23 UTC — resumed the P18-V01 MessageDecoder compatibility slice.

Added a direct pinned-Java fixture invocation for each generic MessageDecoder
decode overload and both clientDecode readBody variants across eleven stored
records, including an empty-body record. The first Rust differential exposed
two behavior differences: Java leaves body null when body reading is disabled
or the encoded body length is zero, and leaves properties null when the record
has no properties section. Rust decoding now preserves both nullable states.

